      <title>Reopening Assessment Twice on Same Issue Unconstitutional, Hits Articles 14 &amp;amp; 300A: Delhi HC in NDTv Founders’ Case [Read Judgment]</title>
      <link>https://www.taxscan.in/top-stories/reopening-assessment-twice-on-same-issue-unconstitutional-hits-articles-14-300a-delhi-hc-in-ndtv-founders-case-1442096</link>
      <description>According to the Delhi High Court, Section 2(22)(e) and Section 2(24)(iv) are two sides of the same coin, and once the transaction had been scrutinised earlier, the Department cannot reopen the case again for the same year on the same subject matter.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.taxscan.in/top-stories/reopening-assessment-twice-on-same-issue-unconstitutional-hits-articles-14-300a-delhi-hc-in-ndtv-founders-case-1442096</guid>
